      "retweet": {
        "id": "2081162179282391307",
        "text": "It’s counter intuitive, but birth rate falls when a civilization grows wealthy\n\nThis is disastrous and has ended great civilizations \n\nWe are not immune from this fate https://t.co/6AbWzgkJzV",
        "created_at": "Sat Jul 25 23:38:24 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "media": [
          {
            "type": "photo",
            "id": "2081162175625015296",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HOHF-OYbsAAP2Mk.jpg"
          }
        ],
        "retweet": null,
        "quoted": {
          "id": "2081161498588496106",
          "text": "A low birth rate due to extended periods of prosperity and low perceived external danger is the primary reason that Rome and most other powerful civilizations collapsed. \n\nRome had a very high birth rate when under extreme pressure from Carthage and a low birth rate a few generations after Carthage, their last serious threat, was finally destroyed.",
